System.assert('a' == 'A');
System.assert(s < 'b');
System.assert(!(s > 'b'));
```

Although `s` `<` `'b'` evaluates to `true` in the example above, `'b.'` `compareTo(s)` generates an error because you’re trying to compare a letter to a `null` value. Naming Conventions

